  "_note": "Build-ready part lists for the four Meadow species. Origin = ground point under the creature; +y up; the creature FACES -z (Roblox front). Units: studs and degrees. CreatureKit builds these 1:1; tools/render_refs.js renders the reference images from this same file.",
  "conventions": {
    "shapes": {
      "ellipsoid": "Part (Block, any size >= 0.05, CanCollide false) with a child SpecialMesh{MeshType=Sphere}; set Mesh.Scale so the visible ellipsoid measures `size`. Do NOT rely on Shape=Ball with a non-uniform Size: verify in Studio how b1b62fd's non-uniform Ball parts actually render before reusing that approach.",
      "block": "Part, Shape=Block, Size=size",
      "cylinder": "Part, Shape=Cylinder. In this file a cylinder's axis is local Y and size = [diameter, height, diameter]; Roblox cylinders run along X, so the builder sets Size=(height, diameter, diameter) and pre-rotates 90 degrees about Z"
    },
    "colors": {"body": "species palette.body", "accent": "species palette.accent", "bodyDark": "body lerped 30% toward ink", "ink": [27, 36, 64], "white": [255, 249, 231], "gold": [255, 217, 90], "blush": [255, 150, 170]},
    "material": "SmoothPlastic for every part; CastShadow true only on the part named body",
    "root": "one extra invisible anchored Root part at the origin (not counted in `parts`); every listed part is unanchored, Massless, CanCollide/CanTouch/CanQuery false, and welded to Root",
    "animation": "squash and stretch = SpecialMesh.Scale and Mesh.Offset on ellipsoids (no Size writes, no physics); whole-creature motion = one Root:PivotTo per frame; ears and wings = Weld.C0 rotation",
    "lod": "`parts` are always present. `nearDetail` parts exist only for the 8 creatures nearest the camera within 35 studs (pooled: 32 parts total)."
